          "topics": "Lariat RNA and spatial transcriptomics crossover; US funding environment; Chinese researchers' rights in the US",
          "notes": "Three main takeaways from the conversation:\n\n1. Lariat RNA pivot: He described how lariat RNA research turned and converged two major schools of spatial transcriptomics, breaking down the barrier between them with an elegant minimal-move approach — \"four taels shifting a thousand pounds\" (四两拨千斤). This was intellectually interesting even though spatial genomics isn't my direction.\n\n2. Funding situation: He indicated that the funding situation in the US is getting better. This is relevant context for PhD application decisions.\n\n3. Politics and Chinese rights: He was notably candid about political topics, especially regarding Chinese researchers' rights in the US. He did not avoid or soft-pedal these issues, which was refreshing and informative.",
